2. In these Regulations —
“Manager” means the Parks and Recreation Agent appointed by the Corporation and includes an authorised officer employed by the agent;
“parks” includes any walk, recreation ground, playground, lake, open space, traffic island and garden maintained by the Manager;
“vehicle” means a vehicle whether mechanically propelled or otherwise.

4. No person shall —
(1)enter or leave a park except through an entrance or exit provided for that purpose;
(2)use or remain in a park except during such hours during which it is open to the public;
(3)affix any bill, placard or notice to or upon any tree, plant, building, barrier, railing, seat, erection, ornament or any wall or fence in or enclosing a park;
(4)enter or remain within a park while under the influence of drugs or in a state of intoxication;
(5)bring or cause to be brought into a park any drugs or any spiritous or intoxicating liquor;
(6)consume any spiritous or intoxicating liquor in a park except in a restaurant or other licensed premises within the grounds of a park;
(7)soil, deface or destroy any building, barrier, railing, post, seat, or any part of any erection or ornament or any implement provided for use in the laying out or maintenance of a park;
(8)climb any wall or fence in or enclosing a park or any tree, barrier, railing, post or other erection;
(9)remove or displace any barrier, railing, post, seat, or any part of any erection or ornament or any implement provided for use in the laying out or maintenance of a park;
(10)remove, cut or displace any soil, turf, plant or tree;
(11)pick any part of any tree, shrub or plant;
(12)throw or discharge any missile in any manner likely to cause or which causes damage to any soil, turf, plant or tree;
(13)bathe, wade or wash in any lake, ornamental lake, fountain, pond or stream, or foul or pollute any water thereof;
(14)capture, injure or destroy or attempt to capture, injure or destroy any fish or water fowl in any such lake, ornamental lake, pond or stream, except in certain areas designed by the Manager for persons to bathe, wade or fish by a notice affixed or set up in some position at or near to each of the areas;
(15)displace, disturb, injure, destroy or take away any bird’s nest or egg;
(16)capture, injure or destroy any bird, butterfly or other insect, or spread, use or set any net, snare or other instrument for the capture, injury or destruction of any bird, butterfly or other insect;
(17)enter any flower-bed or any part of the park which is being prepared as a flower-bed or for other planting;
(18)enter any place where entry is prohibited by a notice placed thereon;
(19)sell, offer or expose for sale, or let to hire, or offer or expose for letting to hire any commodity or article, except in pursuance of a written agreement with the Manager or in the exercise of any lawful right or privilege;
(20)discharge any fireworks, crackers, firearm or weapon;
(21)release any animal;
(22)throw or discharge any stone or missile to the danger of any person, animal, bird, fish, reptile or insect;
(23)preach or deliver any public address or assemble for the purpose of holding or taking part in any social entertainment or any religious, political or other meeting or demonstration of whatever nature;
(24)beat, shake, sweep, brush or cleanse any carpet, rug, mat or any other fabric containing dust or dirt;
(25)wash clothing or other material or hang, spread or deposit any linen or other fabric for drying or bleaching;
(26)deposit litter or refuse, except in litter bins;
(27)undress or be in a state of undress so as to be indecently exposed in the view of the public;
(28)gamble or assist in gambling;
(29)expectorate or use obscene or unbecoming language;
(30)beg, loiter, solicit or commit a nuisance; or
(31)enter or attempt to enter any public convenience provided for the use of the opposite sex.
